Q: Can I execute a function whenever a Python class has its properties changed? A: <p>If you only care about the updating of specific attributes, then I would use a custom-tailored <a href="https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#implementing-descriptors" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><em>data descriptor</em></a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>class MonitoredAttribute:
    def __set_name__(self, owner, name):
        self.public_name = name
        self.private_name = '_' + name

    def __get__(self, instance, owner=None):
        if instance is None:
            return self
        return getattr(instance, self.private_name)

    def __set__(self, instance, value):
        print(f'Setting attribute {self.public_name} to {value!r}')
        setattr(instance, self.private_name, value)

class Foo():
    x = MonitoredAttribute()

    def __init__(self, x):
        self.x = x

foo = Foo(7)
foo.x = 9
</code></pre>
<p>If you cared about <em>any</em> attribute being updated, then I would use <a href="https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__setattr__" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>object.__setattr__</code></a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>class Foo():
    def __init__(self, x):
        self.x = x

    def __setattr__(self, name, value):
       print(f'Setting attribute {name} to {value!r}')
       super().__setattr__(name, value)

foo = Foo(7)
foo.x = 9
</code></pre>

Q: Download a JSON text file in the webpage using only JavaScript/jQuery A: <p>here's what worked for me<br />
I found it on <a href="https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/download-json-file-with-js-p9t1z?file=%2Findex.html%3A40%2C11" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/download-json-file-with-js-p9t1z?file=%2Findex.html%3A40%2C11</a></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button onclick=&quot;onDownload()&quot;&gt;Download&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
    const jsonData = {
      name: &quot;Jhon&quot;,
      email: &quot;Jhon@mail.com&quot;
    };
    function onDownload(){
        const a = document.createElement(&quot;a&quot;);
        const file = new Blob(
                    [JSON.stringify(jsonData)], 
                    {type: &quot;text/plain&quot; });
        a.href = URL.createObjectURL(file);
        a.download = &quot;file.json&quot;;           
                a.click();
    }
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Let helper access private data without modifying header A: <p>If you don't be afraid of black magic, you might do:</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;typename Tag&gt;
struct result {
    friend auto get_type(std::type_identity&lt;result&lt;Tag&gt;&gt;);
};

template&lt;typename Tag, typename HiddenType&gt;
struct rob {
    friend auto get_type(std::type_identity&lt;result&lt;Tag&gt;&gt;) { return std::type_identity&lt;HiddenType&gt;{}; }
};

// And then
class workerTag{};
template struct rob&lt;workerTag, worker::cache_item&gt;; // Private type in explicit instantiation allowed
using exposed_cache_item = typename decltype(get_type(std::type_identity&lt;result&lt;workerTag&gt;&gt;{}))::type;
</code></pre>
